# What the routine searches for. Edit freely; the routine re-reads this every run.
# Generated by Applaut from your profile on {{GENERATED_ON}}. The sources below are for jobs in
# Germany (Federal Employment Agency, Arbeitnow, German job boards); change `locations` and
# `sources` if you search elsewhere.

# Search seeds. Eligibility is decided by each posting's actual tech stack,
# not by its title, so any family here can still be rejected or accepted.
role_families:
{{ROLE_FAMILIES}}

# Skill-led search terms (tools employers put in titles and descriptions).
skill_terms:
{{SKILL_TERMS}}

# German titles employers use for the same roles. Search these too: many German
# companies only post German titles even when the job is in English.
search_terms_de:
{{SEARCH_TERMS_DE}}

# Anywhere in Germany, plus remote roles open to Germany-based candidates.
# Reject only postings located outside Germany that are not remote-from-Germany.
locations:
  scope: germany
  remote_in_germany: true

posted_within_days: 7
min_match_score: 70          # % of must-have skills matched
# Safety ceiling, not a target: documents for more jobs than this in one run risk lower quality.
max_new_jobs_per_run: 50
# One "search" = one search query (an API list call or a web search). Fetching a posting's
# details does not count. Thoroughness matters more than speed: use the budget.
max_searches_per_run: 250

seniority_allowed: [junior, mid, senior]
seniority_excluded_keywords: [Lead, Principal, Head of, Director, Staff, Architect (10+ years)]

excluded_companies: []       # e.g. [Some Company GmbH]
excluded_keywords: [Werkstudent, Working Student, Praktikum, Internship, Ausbildung, Minijob, Freelance]

# Links: at least one of jd_url / application_url must open the specific posting
# (not a homepage or a general careers page). An Arbeitsagentur or job-board page for
# that exact posting is fine. pipeline.py merge rejects jobs that have neither.

sources:
  - name: Bundesagentur für Arbeit Jobsuche API (largest source, use first and exhaustively)
    how: >
      GET https://rest.arbeitsagentur.de/jobboerse/jobsuche-service/pc/v6/jobs
      (v4 returns 403) with header "X-API-Key: jobboerse-jobsuche" and params was=<term>,
      veroeffentlichtseit=<posted_within_days>, size=200, page=<n>, arbeitszeit=vz (full-time).
      Leave out "wo" to search all of Germany. Page until a page returns fewer than size results.
      Run every role family and every search_terms_de entry, plus every skill_terms entry.
      Results are in "ergebnisliste"; useful fields: stellenangebotsTitel, firma, referenznummer,
      stellenlokationen, datumErsteVeroeffentlichung, arbeitszeitVollzeit, homeofficemoeglich.
      Full description (JSON, field stellenangebotsBeschreibung): GET
      https://rest.arbeitsagentur.de/jobboerse/jobsuche-service/pc/v4/jobdetails/<base64 of referenznummer>
      with the same header (v6 jobdetails returns 403).
      Job detail page (valid jd_url): https://www.arbeitsagentur.de/jobsuche/jobdetail/<referenznummer>
  - name: Arbeitnow job board API (Germany, many English-language tech jobs)
    how: >
      GET https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api?page=<n> (JSON; fields title, company_name,
      location, remote, tags, url, created_at as unix time). Page until postings are older than
      posted_within_days. Listings can be stale: confirm the posting is still live.
  - name: ATS job boards (employer postings)
    how: >
      Discover companies with web searches like "site:<domain> <term> Germany" (also try Berlin,
      München, Hamburg, Frankfurt, Köln, remote) for each domain below, then read the board's
      public API or page:
      job-boards.greenhouse.io / boards.greenhouse.io -> https://boards-api.greenhouse.io/v1/boards/<board>/jobs?content=true;
      jobs.lever.co -> https://api.lever.co/v0/postings/<company>?mode=json;
      jobs.personio.de / jobs.personio.com -> https://<company>.jobs.personio.de/xml;
      jobs.smartrecruiters.com -> https://api.smartrecruiters.com/v1/companies/<company>/postings?q=<term>;
      jobs.ashbyhq.com -> https://api.ashbyhq.com/posting-api/job-board/<company>;
      <company>.recruitee.com -> https://<company>.recruitee.com/api/offers;
      apply.workable.com -> https://apply.workable.com/api/v3/accounts/<company>/jobs;
      myworkdayjobs.com, join.com, <company>.teamtailor.com, successfactors career sites: open the posting page.
  - name: German tech job boards
    how: >
      germantechjobs.de and englishjobs.de (browse or web-search "site:<domain> <term>"). Follow each
      hit to the posting; a specific job-board posting page is an acceptable jd_url.
  - name: General web search and company career pages
    how: >
      Search "<term> Germany" / "<term> Deutschland" postings from the last week, plus skill-led
      queries ("<skill> <role> Deutschland", "<skill> Entwickler").
      Open the company's own career page for the posting when it exists.
  - name: Job aggregators (discovery only)
    how: >
      Indeed, StepStone, LinkedIn, Glassdoor, XING results may be used to DISCOVER a job; then find the
      same posting on the employer's site, the Arbeitsagentur or another open page. Never log in.
